<title>PERU: Peru's September cotton output falls 19.2 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's September cotton output falls 19.2 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's September cotton production fell 19.2 percent to 19,398 tonnes, compared with the same month last year, the Agriculture Ministry said Monday.</p>
<p>Output in the first nine months rose 19.0 percent to 244,658, compared with the same period in 1995, the ministry said.</p>
<p>Total 1995 production was 216,869 tonnes.</p>
<p>Imports of uncombed cotton in September fell 59.6 percent to 779.9 tonnes, worth $1.243 million, while imports in the first nine months dropped 44.9 percent to 8,952 tonnes, worth $14.823 million.</p>
<p>There were no export figures for September</p>
<p>-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
